      "evidence": "retain_failures calls row.get and then result.get without a per-row exception boundary. One list/scalar returned_result raises and exits the entire method via the outer operation-level handler. strict_records records malformed inputs but does not add a structurally valid later failed/ABORTED action to original_failures. Later methods do not restore the omitted failure.",
